  "abilities": {
    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Yao Huang ties it to the law of life and death, presenting it as a way for immortal zombies to regain life and leave zombie status, and as a means for him to extend his own lifespan when lifespan Gu are hard to find.",
        "chapters": [
          757
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_lifespan_gu"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "feeding": {
    "known": false,
    "food_raw": null,
    "foods": [],
    "claims": []
  },
  "refinement": {
    "recipes": [],
    "used_in_recipes": [],
    "refinement_materials": [],
    "confirmed_evolutions": [],
    "related_variants": [],
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "An important stage needs a formless vessel as the container. That vessel must be formless and ethereal, with no five elements, light, or darkness, so fire, ice, wood, metal, qi, and similar paths will not work. Yao Huang ranks phantom path best for that vessel, then strength path, space path, and rule path. He buys Cauldron Strength Immortal Gu as that vessel and plans to raise it from rank six to rank seven to improve his odds.",
        "chapters": [
          757
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "refinement-materials",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "path_strength",
          "gu_cauldron_strength_immortal_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Refinement also needs materials that can interact with life and death dao marks. Immortal zombies are the most optimal material, and ten immortal zombies are the least required. Yao Huang claims thirty percent confidence of refining it successfully after years of collaboration with Zombie Alliance using immortal zombies as test subjects on the law of life and death.",
        "chapters": [
          757
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "refinement-materials",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_refinement",
          "sys_immortal_zombie",
          "fac_zombie_alliance"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Northern Plains rumors assign the unfinished Gu a rank eight grade,",
        "chapters": [
          1131
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "rank-rumors-and-refinement",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "and Yao Huang keeps putting refinement ahead of other conflicts.",
        "chapters": [
          1144
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "rank-rumors-and-refinement",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Northern Plains Gu Immortal rumors call resurrection from the dead Immortal Gu rank eight while Yao Huang is still trying to refine it.",
        "chapters": [
          1131
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "rank-rumors-and-refinement",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_immortal"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Yao Huang himself treats finishing the refinement as a way to possess a rank eight Immortal Gu and solve his lifespan problem, and later keeps focusing on that work instead of fighting Old Ancestor Xue Hu.",
        "chapters": [
          1144
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "rank-rumors-and-refinement",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_old_ancestor_xue_hu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "He remains busy with the same refinement when Longevity Heaven presses him into other conflicts.",
        "chapters": [
          1190
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "rank-rumors-and-refinement",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_longevity_heaven"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Heavenly Lord Bai Zu later judges from Yao Huang’s improved gold leaf tea that Yao Huang is not far from refining resurrection from the dead Gu, and that improvement comes from those refinement attempts.",
        "chapters": [
          1235
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "rank-rumors-and-refinement",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_heavenly_lord_bai_zu"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
